<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statuto Albertino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Albertine Statute</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Statuto Albertino was the constitution granted by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-albert-of-sardinia">Charles Albert of Sardinia</a> in March 1848. It created a parliament with an elected chamber and an appointed senate while leaving the king wide powers. After unification in 1861 it became the constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a>, and it remained formally in force, though hollowed out under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a>, until the republican constitution of 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statuto-albertino.jpg" alt="Statuto Albertino" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlo_Alberto_firma_lo_Statuto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
